# Persian typography (inbox)

FA-first product. Apply digit/bidi/spacing cleanup everywhere (including Canva frames and calendars). Do **not** change fonts, Outfit, Canva sizes/leading, or brand-book look.

## Fonts (do not change)

- RTL body/UI: `Vazirmatn Variable` in `app/assets/css/main.css` (`font-display: optional`).
- LTR / Latin brand: `Outfit Variable` via `[dir='ltr']` / `InboxWordmark`.
- Do not swap fonts, remove Outfit, introduce Inter/Geist/Roboto/`system-ui`-only stacks, or commercial fonts (IRANSans, Yekan, Dana).
- Do not change `font-display: optional` to `swap`.
- Do not use Next.js `next/font` — this is Nuxt + `@fontsource-variable/*`.

## Digits & formatters

- User-visible numbers/times/phones/prices/WhatsApp: Persian digits via `useFormatters()` (`formatNumber`, `formatCurrency`, `formatPhone`, `formatTimeLabel`, `formatFaDigits`, …) or `toPersianDigits` from `#shared/jalali.ts`.
- Keep Latin digits in values, `v-model`, `tel:` / `mailto:` hrefs, URLs, codes, version strings.
- Prices/tables/counters: `tabular-nums`.
- Do not invent `fa()` / VibeFarsi helpers.

## Bidi & mixed text

- Page stays `dir="rtl"`. Never set `dir="ltr"` on a whole Persian paragraph.
- Phones, times, SKUs, URLs, codes: `<bdi dir="ltr">` (or `dir="ltr"` on the control).
- Latin brand / wordmark stays `dir="ltr"` with Latin case.

## Spacing (cleanup only — not a redesign)

- `letter-spacing: 0` on Persian text. Never `tracking-tight` / `tracking-wide` / `uppercase` on Persian labels or table headers.
- Exception: Latin-only brand/wordmark and LTR OTP/PIN digit entry may use tracking.
- Prefer `text-start` and logical `ms`/`me`/`gap-*`; avoid `text-right` and physical `ml`/`mr` for alignment.
- Truncate with `line-clamp-*` / `truncate`; do not `slice()` Persian for display.
- `break-all` only on LTR mono codes; never on Persian prose.

## Explicit non-goals

- Do not raise Canva caption sizes, loosen calendar leading, or restyle phone frames to match prose tables.
- Canva Phone Frames LOCKED still wins for chrome, radius, and layout.
- Digit/bidi/spacing fixes on those surfaces are required; visual redesign is not.
